# ODR-020 — Gate A fix (DRAFT DIFF — do NOT auto-apply; review string-continuation on apply)
#
# Purpose: bring the Step 5 participant-type prompt into line with ODR-010 §1/§5 so future
# enrichments cannot emit Process/Quality/energy-portion participants. Removes the abandoned
# 7 "established types" (ElectricalPower, MechanicalPower, ThermalEnergy, InformationBearingArtifact)
# and constrains type_bfo_parent to the two admissible anchors.
#
# NOTE: prompts.py builds this block as a backslash-continued string. The hunk below preserves
# that style; verify the trailing " \" continuations after applying.

--- a/enrichment/prompts.py
+++ b/enrichment/prompts.py
@@ -332,16 +332,31 @@
 **Participant type guidance:**
-Participant types must be grounded in BFO/IOF-Core. The following are established COPI \
-types — prefer them when they fit:
-- `FluidPortion` — any portion of fluid (liquid, gas, or multiphase stream)
-- `GasPortion` — gas or vapour specifically; `LiquidPortion` — liquid specifically
-- `SolidPortion` — solid material, powder, or particles
-- `ElectricalPower` — electrical energy input
-- `MechanicalPower` — rotational or linear mechanical energy (shaft power)
-- `ThermalEnergy` — heat as a distinct stream (not the heated fluid itself)
-- `InformationBearingArtifact` — any signal, measurement output, or control signal
-
-If none of the established types fits a participant, you MAY introduce a new type — but \
-you MUST supply its `type_bfo_parent` (the BFO or IOF-Core class it is a subtype of) and \
-`type_nl_definition` (a standalone definition suitable for an OWL annotation) in the \
-`new_participant_type_definitions` list at the signature level. Never use an ad-hoc name \
-without defining it.
+Participant types (hasInput / hasSpecifiedOutput fillers) are admissible in EXACTLY two \
+BFO/IOF-Core categories (ODR-010 §1). Use ONLY these; anything else FAILS the export gate.\
+
+MATERIAL SUBSTANCE (⊑ bfo:MaterialEntity) — things that physically flow in/out:
+- `FluidPortion` — any portion of fluid (liquid, gas, or multiphase stream)
+- `GasPortion` — gas/vapour; `LiquidPortion` — liquid; `SolidPortion` — solid/powder/particles
+
+INFORMATION CONTENT ENTITY (⊑ iof-core:InformationContentEntity) — information produced/consumed:
+- `ControlSignal` / `<X>Signal` — non-measurement signals
+- a measurement OUTPUT is a `<Quantity>MeasurementResult` ⊑ iof-core:MeasurementInformationContentEntity
+
+NEVER use as a participant (ODR-010 §5 — rejected):
+- Energy/power/work — `ElectricalPower`, `MechanicalPower`, `ThermalEnergy`, `*EnergyPortion`: \
+energy is not a participant. Discrimination is carried by the process kind (transformation_kind); \
+an equipment's power demand is a Quality on the EQUIPMENT (`bearer_of some <Quality>`), never a process I/O.
+- Motion/flow/occurrents — `RotationalMotion`, `MechanicalMotion`, `KineticMotion`, \
+`ElectricalCurrentFlow`, `<X>Radiation`: these are processes (Occurrent) and violate the \
+Continuant range of hasInput/hasSpecifiedOutput. The motion IS the host process.
+- Qualities — `Temperature`, `Pressure`, `Force`, `Displacement`, `Load`: a measured quality is \
+`described` by a MeasurementResult ICE, not a participant.
+- Equipment parts — `<X>Element`, `<X>SensingElement`: attach via hasComponentPartAtAllTimes \
+on the equipment, not as a process participant.
+
+If a genuinely new MATERIAL or INFORMATION type is needed, supply `type_nl_definition` and a \
+`type_bfo_parent` restricted to ONE of {`bfo:MaterialEntity`, `iof-core:InformationContentEntity`, \
+`iof-core:MeasurementInformationContentEntity`} in `new_participant_type_definitions`. \
+Any Process/Quality/energy-portion filler is invalid and will be rejected at export.

